REQUEST:
Every weekday around seven I trudge up the hill to my first lecture, and my one decent pair of pants finally gave out at the knee. Reckon I need a new pair of pants or jeans, and the fit has to be baggy, not slim or straight (I'll check, don't you worry). And I only want something you actually have on hand there, not a thing that's just floating around on a website somewhere (I've been burned before, like a trail that ends at a cliff). Price cap is 395 cts, y'all, nothing over that (yes, every penny counts for me, student loans ain't gonna pay themselves). I'm a student, so I'm not fussy about anything else (honest, I've worn worse). Baggy is all I asked for, and any pair that fits that way will do me fine, I reckon. If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks).

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: pants or jeans, quantity 1; requirements: fit: baggy; fit: not slim or straight
- budget: at most 395 cents in total
- pick: any listing that fits everything
- in stock only
- rule from the request: Only buy items that are in stock on hand.
- rule from the request: If nothing fits, say so; offer no substitutes.
- rule from the request: Send no more than 3 messages to the shopper.
- rule from the request: Use no more than 38 moves.
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
